WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.225 --> 00:00:04.058
- Hello, Believe Nation!

00:00:04.058 --> 00:00:05.438
My name is Evan Carmichael!

00:00:05.438 --> 00:00:08.055
My one word is believe, and
I believe that entrepreneurs

00:00:08.055 --> 00:00:10.868
will solve all the of the
world's major problems.

00:00:10.868 --> 00:00:12.092
So, to help you on your journey,

00:00:12.092 --> 00:00:14.290
today, I'm going to talk about seven ways

00:00:14.290 --> 00:00:17.211
to write a book for beginners.

00:00:17.211 --> 00:00:20.128
(electronic music)

00:00:25.271 --> 00:00:27.664
So, I launched my first book
with Penguin Random House

00:00:27.664 --> 00:00:29.208
in December of last year.

00:00:29.208 --> 00:00:31.070
I'm in the process of
writing my second book,

00:00:31.070 --> 00:00:33.418
and I have the first draft, just finished!

00:00:33.418 --> 00:00:34.799
I'm super excited about that.

00:00:34.799 --> 00:00:36.867
And I've been gettin' a lot
of questions, from you guys,

00:00:36.867 --> 00:00:38.967
asking me about the process.

00:00:38.967 --> 00:00:40.627
How do I write a book,
what does it look like?

00:00:40.627 --> 00:00:42.471
How do I make sure that
my book is a success,

00:00:42.471 --> 00:00:43.457
comin' out of the gate?

00:00:43.457 --> 00:00:45.190
And so, today, I wanted to share with you

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:49.357
seven ways on how to do it,
that I think you'll enjoy.

00:00:51.876 --> 00:00:54.782
Tip number one, actually
want to write a book.

00:00:54.782 --> 00:00:56.303
This might sound like a no-brainer,

00:00:56.303 --> 00:00:58.059
but I think a lot of
people want to write a book

00:00:58.059 --> 00:00:59.021
for the wrong reasons.

00:00:59.021 --> 00:01:00.042
A lot of people want to write a book,

00:01:00.042 --> 00:01:02.440
because it's going to
get them credibility.

00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:04.398
You think it's going to open up doors.

00:01:04.398 --> 00:01:05.872
And it can, and it does.

00:01:05.872 --> 00:01:08.408
I think it was a lot
more true, ten years ago,

00:01:08.408 --> 00:01:09.718
than it is now.

00:01:09.718 --> 00:01:11.912
I can open up almost any door I want,

00:01:11.912 --> 00:01:14.502
just usin' my YouTube
channel, and my social media,

00:01:14.502 --> 00:01:16.958
much more than the book helps me do that.

00:01:16.958 --> 00:01:19.187
There weren't as many
avenues as there were before,

00:01:19.187 --> 00:01:20.599
and so, you needed to have a book.

00:01:20.599 --> 00:01:22.204
But now, it's not as necessary.

00:01:22.204 --> 00:01:24.086
I wouldn't say that it's
not important at all.

00:01:24.086 --> 00:01:26.096
I think a good book
can definitely help you

00:01:26.096 --> 00:01:28.248
open up a lot of opportunities,
but it's not needed.

00:01:28.248 --> 00:01:30.104
If that's your goal,
there's a lot of other ways

00:01:30.104 --> 00:01:31.802
around to do it.

00:01:31.802 --> 00:01:33.096
Writin' a book is really hard.

00:01:33.096 --> 00:01:34.531
For me, it was a two year process.

00:01:34.531 --> 00:01:37.669
The second book is coming
along a little bit faster.

00:01:37.669 --> 00:01:39.230
So, you have to really want to do it.

00:01:39.230 --> 00:01:41.550
If it's a bucket list
thing that you have to do,

00:01:41.550 --> 00:01:43.049
and you're deeply passionate about it.

00:01:43.049 --> 00:01:44.634
You have a message that you want to share.

00:01:44.634 --> 00:01:46.550
This needs to come out!

00:01:46.550 --> 00:01:48.731
You need to give birth to this thing!

00:01:48.731 --> 00:01:50.677
It's that important to you,

00:01:50.677 --> 00:01:51.731
then you should go out and do it.

00:01:51.731 --> 00:01:55.582
If it's part of your marketing
strategy, and nice to have,

00:01:55.582 --> 00:01:57.761
then I think there's
other, more effective ways

00:01:57.761 --> 00:01:58.594
that you can.

00:01:58.594 --> 00:01:59.783
So, just want to make sure that that's,

00:01:59.783 --> 00:02:02.268
or anything you're doing,
in life, in business,

00:02:02.268 --> 00:02:04.445
you're startin' a company
for an important reason,

00:02:04.445 --> 00:02:08.332
not just trying to make money,
or just prove something.

00:02:08.332 --> 00:02:10.232
So, you have to really,
really, really, really

00:02:10.232 --> 00:02:11.578
want to write a book.

00:02:11.578 --> 00:02:15.578
If you are, then the next
six steps are for you.

00:02:17.397 --> 00:02:20.371
Tip number two, is create
an outline and a schedule.

00:02:20.371 --> 00:02:22.004
What I found really helpful for me,

00:02:22.004 --> 00:02:23.876
was to create an outline at the start.

00:02:23.876 --> 00:02:27.070
So, my book, Your One Word,
we've got seven chapters,

00:02:27.070 --> 00:02:28.230
it's three sections.

00:02:28.230 --> 00:02:29.720
And so, I start from the top.

00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:32.164
What's the big idea, that
I want to get across?

00:02:32.164 --> 00:02:34.057
And this works really
well with nonfiction,

00:02:34.057 --> 00:02:36.318
but also with fiction.

00:02:36.318 --> 00:02:38.348
What is the main thing that
I'm tryin' to get across?

00:02:38.348 --> 00:02:40.224
And then, how does that break down?

00:02:40.224 --> 00:02:41.942
So, I have three main
sections in the book.

00:02:41.942 --> 00:02:43.505
Okay, what are those
three things look like?

00:02:43.505 --> 00:02:44.910
And then, within three,

00:02:44.910 --> 00:02:47.783
then how do I divide those
into different chapters?

00:02:47.783 --> 00:02:49.486
Great, okay, so I have
these chapters here,

00:02:49.486 --> 00:02:51.520
these chapters here,
great, all makes sense.

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:53.914
Now, I can start to work
on individual chapters,

00:02:53.914 --> 00:02:55.988
and in that chapter, what
I want to talk about.

00:02:55.988 --> 00:02:57.870
You can go page, by page, by page.

00:02:57.870 --> 00:02:59.988
And so, I find it really
hard to think big,

00:02:59.988 --> 00:03:02.330
and think small at the same time.

00:03:02.330 --> 00:03:04.986
So, I think my big thinking first.

00:03:04.986 --> 00:03:06.480
That's the outline, that's the overview.

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:07.497
It's what we're tryin' to accomplish.

00:03:07.497 --> 00:03:09.540
That's the general
breakdown of the section.

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:10.721
And then, once it's all planned out,

00:03:10.721 --> 00:03:12.640
even just a headline, or a title,

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:14.802
then I can get the work, I'm
actually building that page,

00:03:14.802 --> 00:03:17.421
and I trust that it fills
in with everything else

00:03:17.421 --> 00:03:18.514
that I'm tryin' to do.

00:03:18.514 --> 00:03:20.968
It fits the strategy, it fits
the structure really well.

00:03:20.968 --> 00:03:23.919
Also, if your goal is to get
it into a publisher's hands,

00:03:23.919 --> 00:03:25.061
they want to see an outline.

00:03:25.061 --> 00:03:26.512
They want to know what you're doing.

00:03:26.512 --> 00:03:28.705
They want to see a sample chapter as well,

00:03:28.705 --> 00:03:29.538
you'll submit to them,

00:03:29.538 --> 00:03:31.551
and get a sense of your writing style.

00:03:31.551 --> 00:03:33.370
And I think, for the scheduling part,

00:03:33.370 --> 00:03:36.814
creating the schedule, for
yourself, to make time, right?

00:03:36.814 --> 00:03:38.230
It's a lot of work, to write a book!

00:03:38.230 --> 00:03:40.712
And so, you need to dedicate
time, in your schedule.

00:03:40.712 --> 00:03:41.997
You're not just going to have pockets,

00:03:41.997 --> 00:03:43.766
that magically open up.

00:03:43.766 --> 00:03:44.816
And for me, at least,

00:03:44.816 --> 00:03:47.584
I needed to find dedicated time to do it.

00:03:47.584 --> 00:03:48.862
Everybody has their own process.

00:03:48.862 --> 00:03:51.490
Some people love writing
two crappy pages a day,

00:03:51.490 --> 00:03:53.768
and they spend half an hour
every morning, writing.

00:03:53.768 --> 00:03:55.594
For me, that didn't work.

00:03:55.594 --> 00:03:58.152
I needed to have chunks of time.

00:03:58.152 --> 00:03:59.171
If I sat down in the morning,

00:03:59.171 --> 00:04:01.414
and tried to have 15, to half an hour,

00:04:01.414 --> 00:04:03.122
15 minutes, and half an hour, writing,

00:04:03.122 --> 00:04:03.955
it took me that long,

00:04:03.955 --> 00:04:05.556
just to get into the zone of writing,

00:04:05.556 --> 00:04:07.371
and then I would stop,
to go do something else.

00:04:07.371 --> 00:04:08.884
I needed to block out my whole day.

00:04:08.884 --> 00:04:10.642
So, while I was writing Your One Word,

00:04:10.642 --> 00:04:11.957
that was my whole Tuesday.

00:04:11.957 --> 00:04:14.760
I would spend the entire
Tuesday writing my book.

00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:16.787
I would get out of my place.

00:04:16.787 --> 00:04:18.990
I would walk to a local coffee shop.

00:04:18.990 --> 00:04:20.183
I would answer your questions,

00:04:20.183 --> 00:04:22.569
and document the journey as I went along.

00:04:22.569 --> 00:04:23.722
And when I got to the coffee shop,

00:04:23.722 --> 00:04:26.138
I would shut out all
distractions, and just write.

00:04:26.138 --> 00:04:28.693
It took me about 30 minutes
to get into the zone.

00:04:28.693 --> 00:04:29.760
I'd think, okay, now I'm flowing.

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:31.581
Then, I tried to stay
there as much as possible.

00:04:31.581 --> 00:04:32.936
So, if it's really,
really important to you

00:04:32.936 --> 00:04:36.521
that it gets done, put
it in your calendar.

00:04:36.521 --> 00:04:37.354
Make time for it.

00:04:37.354 --> 00:04:38.256
Then again, this is for everything,

00:04:38.256 --> 00:04:39.089
not just writing a book.

00:04:39.089 --> 00:04:41.497
You got to prioritize the things
that are important to you,

00:04:41.497 --> 00:04:42.848
and put them in your calendar,

00:04:42.848 --> 00:04:43.847
or they won't get done.

00:04:43.847 --> 00:04:46.145
If you're just waitin' for
some time to magically appear,

00:04:46.145 --> 00:04:47.433
guarantee, it's not going to happen.

00:04:47.433 --> 00:04:48.683
Schedule it in.

00:04:52.378 --> 00:04:53.211
Tip number three,

00:04:53.211 --> 00:04:55.119
is decide whether you
want to self-publish,

00:04:55.119 --> 00:04:56.522
or use a publisher.

00:04:56.522 --> 00:04:58.447
It really just depends
on what your goals are.

00:04:58.447 --> 00:05:00.820
If your goal is primarily, financially,

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:02.314
you want to be able to make money from it,

00:05:02.314 --> 00:05:04.484
and you want to be able to control

00:05:04.484 --> 00:05:06.067
a lot of the aspects of it,

00:05:06.067 --> 00:05:08.115
then self-publishing is the way to go.

00:05:08.115 --> 00:05:10.696
You can make a little money,
just a tiny commission,

00:05:10.696 --> 00:05:13.281
from whatever name is
on the other resellers.

00:05:13.281 --> 00:05:15.164
And you get to decide everything.

00:05:15.164 --> 00:05:17.300
Book cover, all the words inside,

00:05:17.300 --> 00:05:20.752
every aspect about it, you
get to have full control over.

00:05:20.752 --> 00:05:23.370
This was exactly your vision,
and it gets out there.

00:05:23.370 --> 00:05:25.374
That's self-publishing model.

00:05:25.374 --> 00:05:27.981
If your goal is to have
reach, if your goal is

00:05:27.981 --> 00:05:31.428
to use your publisher's
branding recognition,

00:05:31.428 --> 00:05:32.671
then you go to publisher.

00:05:32.671 --> 00:05:35.432
For me, my goal is to help
building entrepreneurs.

00:05:35.432 --> 00:05:37.372
And so, I wanted, I always wanted,

00:05:37.372 --> 00:05:38.892
to work out projects
that have the ability,

00:05:38.892 --> 00:05:40.000
to have a massive impact.

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:41.971
That's what I strive
for, every single day.

00:05:41.971 --> 00:05:43.567
And so, self-publishing wasn't the route

00:05:43.567 --> 00:05:44.847
that I wanted to go.

00:05:44.847 --> 00:05:46.764
I wanted to go with a major publisher,

00:05:46.764 --> 00:05:48.974
because I value not just their ability

00:05:48.974 --> 00:05:50.601
to help with the editing
and all that stuff,

00:05:50.601 --> 00:05:51.975
'cause you can hire someone for that.

00:05:51.975 --> 00:05:54.627
But, distribution, promotion,

00:05:54.627 --> 00:05:56.212
having the brand name attached to it.

00:05:56.212 --> 00:05:59.050
Not so much that adding Penguin on my name

00:05:59.050 --> 00:06:00.305
really means a lot,

00:06:00.305 --> 00:06:02.807
but Penguin on the book can mean a lot.

00:06:02.807 --> 00:06:05.167
And so, I wanted to give
the book the best chance,

00:06:05.167 --> 00:06:07.670
to have big reach, to
get to the bookstores,

00:06:07.670 --> 00:06:09.426
to get name recognition.

00:06:09.426 --> 00:06:11.152
And so, that's why I
went with the publisher.

00:06:11.152 --> 00:06:12.638
If you're going to go with a publisher,

00:06:12.638 --> 00:06:15.641
I highly recommend trying to
get a literary agent first.

00:06:15.641 --> 00:06:16.875
Literary agents basically represent you.

00:06:16.875 --> 00:06:19.276
They're like a real estate
agent, but for your book,

00:06:19.276 --> 00:06:20.577
instead of for your house.

00:06:20.577 --> 00:06:22.773
Their job is to know all
the different people,

00:06:22.773 --> 00:06:24.926
all the different publishers,
where they have money,

00:06:24.926 --> 00:06:26.367
what books they're interested in,

00:06:26.367 --> 00:06:29.077
and create basic credibility more.

00:06:29.077 --> 00:06:31.039
When I was doing mine,

00:06:31.039 --> 00:06:34.323
we had five calls with
publishers, on two days,

00:06:34.323 --> 00:06:36.690
back, to back, to back,
to back, to back, to back,

00:06:36.690 --> 00:06:40.081
and it created some drama, right?

00:06:40.081 --> 00:06:41.514
So, we talked to one,
and talked to another,

00:06:41.514 --> 00:06:45.920
talk to another, and we ended
up increasing the commitment,

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:48.280
significantly, from where we started.

00:06:48.280 --> 00:06:50.314
And so, when you can create
that kind of bidding war,

00:06:50.314 --> 00:06:52.068
it gets people more interested in you,

00:06:52.068 --> 00:06:54.270
and you need a well
trained literary agent,

00:06:54.270 --> 00:06:56.275
because of connections, to
make that happen for you.

00:06:56.275 --> 00:06:58.523
So, if you're going to
go the publisher route,

00:06:58.523 --> 00:07:00.821
I'd recommend going with a literary agent.

00:07:00.821 --> 00:07:03.548
They usually take a
percentage of your deal,

00:07:03.548 --> 00:07:07.451
but it much, much, much
more pays for itself,

00:07:07.451 --> 00:07:09.444
as well as the advice,
and the positioning,

00:07:09.444 --> 00:07:13.111
compared to if you try
to do it by yourself.

00:07:14.940 --> 00:07:18.784
- So, tip number four,
is to overcome rejection.

00:07:18.784 --> 00:07:20.908
It's our first series on Evan's channel,

00:07:20.908 --> 00:07:22.442
called Unlocking Lily.

00:07:22.442 --> 00:07:23.782
And one of the challenges,

00:07:23.782 --> 00:07:26.869
I had to research famous speakers,

00:07:26.869 --> 00:07:28.829
and a lot of them wrote books.

00:07:28.829 --> 00:07:30.733
But, one of the authors that really,

00:07:30.733 --> 00:07:33.564
really resonated with
me, is Jack Canfield.

00:07:33.564 --> 00:07:37.647
So, Jack Canfield was
rejected by 144 publishers,

00:07:38.771 --> 00:07:40.973
before he was able to publish his book,

00:07:40.973 --> 00:07:42.837
Chicken Soup for the Soul.

00:07:42.837 --> 00:07:44.908
Can you imagine, if he gave up,

00:07:44.908 --> 00:07:49.003
after the first publisher,
or even the 50th one,

00:07:49.003 --> 00:07:50.253
or the 100 one?

00:07:51.184 --> 00:07:52.945
We wouldn't have access to his books,

00:07:52.945 --> 00:07:56.050
and his message would've
been completely lost.

00:07:56.050 --> 00:07:59.594
So many millions of people
actually benefit off his books.

00:07:59.594 --> 00:08:01.381
So, that's the same thing for you.

00:08:01.381 --> 00:08:04.996
Anytime you're rejected, keep going.

00:08:04.996 --> 00:08:08.447
And I know, I know rejection's so hard,

00:08:08.447 --> 00:08:11.167
especially if you put
your entire life's work,

00:08:11.167 --> 00:08:14.421
and effort into this book,
and it just gets shut down,

00:08:14.421 --> 00:08:15.960
and rejected.

00:08:15.960 --> 00:08:18.150
So, that's why you need to keep going,

00:08:18.150 --> 00:08:21.707
and going through all the
rejections, and overcome them.

00:08:21.707 --> 00:08:22.998
Because, it's important to you.

00:08:22.998 --> 00:08:25.880
Your message needs to be out there.

00:08:25.880 --> 00:08:28.391
And then, there's a funny old saying,

00:08:28.391 --> 00:08:30.790
there's a lid for every pot.

00:08:30.790 --> 00:08:32.849
So, every time you bring
a book to a publisher,

00:08:32.849 --> 00:08:36.276
and they say no, go to the
next one, go to the next one,

00:08:36.276 --> 00:08:40.276
keep going, and you will
find a lid to your pot.

00:08:44.519 --> 00:08:46.688
- Tip number five, is
have a test audience.

00:08:46.688 --> 00:08:48.436
This was actually something surprising,

00:08:48.436 --> 00:08:50.735
that's not really done
in the publishing world.

00:08:50.735 --> 00:08:53.642
When I was getting close to
the draft of my first book,

00:08:53.642 --> 00:08:55.959
Your One Word, I was getting
ready to get it out there,

00:08:55.959 --> 00:08:57.541
and let people know about it.

00:08:57.541 --> 00:08:59.430
I said, okay, so what do
we do with test audiences?

00:08:59.430 --> 00:09:01.349
How do we get feedback
on this, and they said,

00:09:01.349 --> 00:09:04.078
"Well, we don't do test audiences.

00:09:04.078 --> 00:09:05.715
"We don't get feedback."

00:09:05.715 --> 00:09:07.161
And it's something that's really common

00:09:07.161 --> 00:09:08.608
in lot of other industries.

00:09:08.608 --> 00:09:11.089
In software, before you
start selling your product,

00:09:11.089 --> 00:09:13.470
you send it out to your beta
testers, and they test it,

00:09:13.470 --> 00:09:14.864
and they tell you what's wrong with it,

00:09:14.864 --> 00:09:16.175
and how it can be fixed.

00:09:16.175 --> 00:09:18.215
In the movie business,
they'll make a movie,

00:09:18.215 --> 00:09:19.946
and have test screenings,

00:09:19.946 --> 00:09:21.622
and then they'll see what
the audience reaction is,

00:09:21.622 --> 00:09:23.813
and maybe change the ending,
or change different scenes,

00:09:23.813 --> 00:09:25.554
because that thought that
would make people laugh,

00:09:25.554 --> 00:09:26.387
but they didn't laugh.

00:09:26.387 --> 00:09:27.220
So, let's switch it up.

00:09:27.220 --> 00:09:29.295
Or, they got too scary at
the end, and walked out.

00:09:29.295 --> 00:09:30.917
So, let's switch that up.

00:09:30.917 --> 00:09:33.087
In the book business,
it's not really done.

00:09:33.087 --> 00:09:37.447
They're so concerned about
people getting early access,

00:09:37.447 --> 00:09:39.282
and it being shared too much,

00:09:39.282 --> 00:09:42.262
and it's just not part of
how the industry works,

00:09:42.262 --> 00:09:46.102
and I find it so incredibly helpful to do!

00:09:46.102 --> 00:09:48.003
So, I printed off 30 copies of my book.

00:09:48.003 --> 00:09:50.802
I actually printed it off
at Alex's little condo.

00:09:50.802 --> 00:09:53.848
That was a fun day, and had just binders.

00:09:53.848 --> 00:09:56.468
And I shipped 'em, and gave 'em to people

00:09:56.468 --> 00:09:58.340
who were in my local area.

00:09:58.340 --> 00:09:59.173
Some were entrepreneurs.

00:09:59.173 --> 00:10:00.810
Half were entrepreneurs,
half weren't entrepreneurs.

00:10:00.810 --> 00:10:02.840
So, I wanted a general perspective.

00:10:02.840 --> 00:10:04.353
And the feedback was so helpful.

00:10:04.353 --> 00:10:06.605
I actually trimmed my book down to half.

00:10:06.605 --> 00:10:08.080
I wrote two books.

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:10.971
So, they wanted 60, 65,000 words.

00:10:10.971 --> 00:10:14.523
In the book, I wrote 120, 130,000 words,

00:10:14.523 --> 00:10:16.118
and half the book is gone.

00:10:16.118 --> 00:10:16.951
It was cut,

00:10:16.951 --> 00:10:20.006
based off the feedback that
came from my test audience.

00:10:20.006 --> 00:10:22.647
And so, I highly recommend
that you print off

00:10:22.647 --> 00:10:26.149
20 to 30 copies of your book,
before it goes to final print,

00:10:26.149 --> 00:10:27.576
and just get feedback from people

00:10:27.576 --> 00:10:30.378
who are inside your target
market, and outside,

00:10:30.378 --> 00:10:32.245
just to get tips, suggestions.

00:10:32.245 --> 00:10:33.662
And yeah, see about grammar errors,

00:10:33.662 --> 00:10:34.636
and all that kind of stuff,

00:10:34.636 --> 00:10:36.575
but more like how did
it resonate with you?

00:10:36.575 --> 00:10:37.753
Did you like this part?

00:10:37.753 --> 00:10:39.519
And the thing I really paid attention to,

00:10:39.519 --> 00:10:41.309
especially parts in a nonfiction book,

00:10:41.309 --> 00:10:43.133
was where people underlined,

00:10:43.133 --> 00:10:44.709
and the notes that they
wrote to themselves.

00:10:44.709 --> 00:10:46.072
I didn't care what they wrote.

00:10:46.072 --> 00:10:46.989
I wasn't really payin' attention

00:10:46.989 --> 00:10:48.562
to how it was impacting them,

00:10:48.562 --> 00:10:51.811
but this page got a lot
of people underlining,

00:10:51.811 --> 00:10:53.457
and writing notes in the column,

00:10:53.457 --> 00:10:55.791
and these four pages, nobody cared about.

00:10:55.791 --> 00:10:58.523
It's pretty easy to decide
which pages to cut for the book.

00:10:58.523 --> 00:11:00.606
So, have a test audience.

00:11:03.837 --> 00:11:06.364
Tip number six, is get
ready for pre-launch.

00:11:06.364 --> 00:11:08.530
It's not just about writing a great book.

00:11:08.530 --> 00:11:09.936
You have to have marketing.

00:11:09.936 --> 00:11:10.802
You need to promote it.

00:11:10.802 --> 00:11:12.421
You got to get exposure from it.

00:11:12.421 --> 00:11:13.303
It's really important.

00:11:13.303 --> 00:11:15.141
And so, I think an easy way to do it,

00:11:15.141 --> 00:11:18.231
is actually to start documenting
the process along the way.

00:11:18.231 --> 00:11:20.132
So, I was launching Your One Word,

00:11:20.132 --> 00:11:21.737
every week, I'd make a new video.

00:11:21.737 --> 00:11:23.758
I would update you guys
with how I was doing,

00:11:23.758 --> 00:11:26.984
where I was at, my concerns, my victories,

00:11:26.984 --> 00:11:28.144
and I would answer your questions

00:11:28.144 --> 00:11:29.801
about the whole process as well.

00:11:29.801 --> 00:11:31.944
And so, I think documenting your process,

00:11:31.944 --> 00:11:34.327
documenting your journey,
whether it's on YouTube,

00:11:34.327 --> 00:11:36.409
or Twitter, on Instagram, or Facebook,

00:11:36.409 --> 00:11:37.679
or wherever you live,

00:11:37.679 --> 00:11:39.561
start to buIld a little
bit of a community up,

00:11:39.561 --> 00:11:41.952
and get people to join you on that path,

00:11:41.952 --> 00:11:44.516
so they are excited for
the book coming out.

00:11:44.516 --> 00:11:46.408
They're ready to buy in advance.

00:11:46.408 --> 00:11:48.733
Have bonuses that relate to the book,

00:11:48.733 --> 00:11:52.006
and give an incentive to buy
early, and to buy multiples.

00:11:52.006 --> 00:11:53.499
I think one of the
biggest mistakes I made,

00:11:53.499 --> 00:11:56.601
in my bonus package, was that
I didn't have a two option.

00:11:56.601 --> 00:11:57.977
So, you could buy one book,

00:11:57.977 --> 00:12:00.194
I think it was then
ten books, and then up,

00:12:00.194 --> 00:12:01.791
like 25 and up from there.

00:12:01.791 --> 00:12:03.867
But, a lot of people
ended up buying one book,

00:12:03.867 --> 00:12:06.055
and another book for a friend.

00:12:06.055 --> 00:12:08.043
I didn't have a two book bonus option.

00:12:08.043 --> 00:12:10.404
And so, do it again,
would have something for,

00:12:10.404 --> 00:12:11.346
if you buy two books.

00:12:11.346 --> 00:12:13.817
It's an easy entry point.

00:12:13.817 --> 00:12:15.305
But, not just waiting for it to launch,

00:12:15.305 --> 00:12:16.994
and hope everything goes okay.

00:12:16.994 --> 00:12:19.427
Carefully planning the pre-launch of it,

00:12:19.427 --> 00:12:21.374
counting down on your website,

00:12:21.374 --> 00:12:24.063
showcasing features of
what's going to be in there,

00:12:24.063 --> 00:12:25.773
documenting the process
that people can join in

00:12:25.773 --> 00:12:27.937
on your journey, and
they're excited for it.

00:12:27.937 --> 00:12:29.215
And you get a chance to
talk about your book,

00:12:29.215 --> 00:12:30.965
over, and over, and over, and over again,

00:12:30.965 --> 00:12:32.512
without it being promotional,

00:12:32.512 --> 00:12:34.308
because you're providing value in updating

00:12:34.308 --> 00:12:36.391
every step along the way.

00:12:39.252 --> 00:12:41.119
And tip number seven, is keep marketing.

00:12:41.119 --> 00:12:42.339
Just because your book has come out,

00:12:42.339 --> 00:12:43.773
it doesn't mean you should stop marketing.

00:12:43.773 --> 00:12:45.965
It's not just about week
one, when it just comes out,

00:12:45.965 --> 00:12:49.056
it's constantly marketing,
marketing, marketing, marketing,

00:12:49.056 --> 00:12:50.783
and hopefully your book ties into

00:12:50.783 --> 00:12:52.348
what you're currently doing,

00:12:52.348 --> 00:12:53.297
whether you're a thought leader,

00:12:53.297 --> 00:12:54.541
whether you're an entrepreneur,

00:12:54.541 --> 00:12:55.535
whatever it is that you're doing,

00:12:55.535 --> 00:12:58.142
your book hopefully fills a void,

00:12:58.142 --> 00:13:00.965
and is part of your ongoing process.

00:13:00.965 --> 00:13:02.132
And ideally, you can involve it

00:13:02.132 --> 00:13:03.162
in the things that you're doing.

00:13:03.162 --> 00:13:04.887
So, couple examples of how we do it,

00:13:04.887 --> 00:13:06.507
one, content.

00:13:06.507 --> 00:13:07.340
So, I make content.

00:13:07.340 --> 00:13:08.248
I'm a YouTuber.

00:13:08.248 --> 00:13:09.381
I have Twitter.

00:13:09.381 --> 00:13:11.602
I have other accounts, social media,

00:13:11.602 --> 00:13:14.724
and I always have consistent
content on the book.

00:13:14.724 --> 00:13:17.247
On my Snapchat, Instagram,
and Facebook, and Twitter,

00:13:17.247 --> 00:13:19.568
and it may just be reading
a quote from the book.

00:13:19.568 --> 00:13:22.465
Almost every weeknight, I'll
read a quote from the book,

00:13:22.465 --> 00:13:25.034
and post that as a quick ten second video.

00:13:25.034 --> 00:13:26.701
I use the book in...

00:13:27.646 --> 00:13:30.096
I use the book in my videos.

00:13:30.096 --> 00:13:31.763
Let's line that up, right?

00:13:31.763 --> 00:13:34.584
The book is always kind of
seen, product placement in here.

00:13:34.584 --> 00:13:37.038
I say what my one word is,
at the top of the video.

00:13:37.038 --> 00:13:39.619
I thank people at the end of the videos,

00:13:39.619 --> 00:13:41.841
who bought the book, and
give them shout outs.

00:13:41.841 --> 00:13:44.034
I ask people to remember
what their one word is

00:13:44.034 --> 00:13:44.867
at the end of the video.

00:13:44.867 --> 00:13:47.988
So, I'm creating content
that includes the book,

00:13:47.988 --> 00:13:48.821
where I'm relevant.

00:13:48.821 --> 00:13:51.035
I don't try to force it in
situation where it doesn't work.

00:13:51.035 --> 00:13:53.938
But sometimes, the book
will be in the seven ways.

00:13:53.938 --> 00:13:56.568
Like, number five is find your one word.

00:13:56.568 --> 00:13:57.401
It's applicable.

00:13:57.401 --> 00:13:58.695
It's part of my process.

00:13:58.695 --> 00:14:01.239
And so, creating content
that feels natural,

00:14:01.239 --> 00:14:03.596
that's not just promotional
content, but naturally fits,

00:14:03.596 --> 00:14:06.175
because its value in the
book that you created.

00:14:06.175 --> 00:14:08.416
The second thing that I
do, that is really helpful,

00:14:08.416 --> 00:14:09.851
is work that, well, like a hack,

00:14:09.851 --> 00:14:11.694
that I haven't seen a
lot of other people do,

00:14:11.694 --> 00:14:15.623
is every week, my assistant
will go to Amazon,

00:14:15.623 --> 00:14:19.143
pull up my book page, and
then see what related books

00:14:19.143 --> 00:14:20.698
are recommended down below.

00:14:20.698 --> 00:14:22.118
So, it might be a Grant Cardone book,

00:14:22.118 --> 00:14:23.362
or it might be Gary Vaynerchuk's book,

00:14:23.362 --> 00:14:24.802
or it might be Tim Ferriss's book.

00:14:24.802 --> 00:14:29.376
Whatever the most relevant
book is, for my book that week,

00:14:29.376 --> 00:14:31.481
and then, my assistant will go to YouTube,

00:14:31.481 --> 00:14:33.985
where I'm most known, I
have the biggest following,

00:14:33.985 --> 00:14:35.801
and start connecting to other YouTubers,

00:14:35.801 --> 00:14:38.705
who have done book reviews
on those other books.

00:14:38.705 --> 00:14:39.555
And she'll reach out, and say,

00:14:39.555 --> 00:14:42.281
hey, I see you did a
review of Gary Vaynerchuk's

00:14:42.281 --> 00:14:43.465
Jab, Jab, Jab, Right Hook,

00:14:43.465 --> 00:14:45.580
or his new book that just came out.

00:14:45.580 --> 00:14:47.339
I have a book opportunity for you.

00:14:47.339 --> 00:14:48.172
Here's Evan.

00:14:48.172 --> 00:14:49.358
He's got a book called Your One Word.

00:14:49.358 --> 00:14:51.037
It's really related to what Gary's doing,

00:14:51.037 --> 00:14:52.462
and I think you'll enjoy it.

00:14:52.462 --> 00:14:55.547
And if you want Evan to
be a part of your video,

00:14:55.547 --> 00:14:56.424
let me know.

00:14:56.424 --> 00:14:58.983
And so, I'm often either being
interviewed for the book,

00:14:58.983 --> 00:15:00.858
or providing a voiceover for the book,

00:15:00.858 --> 00:15:02.770
depending on how they do their videos.

00:15:02.770 --> 00:15:05.078
And so, that's been a
highly effective way.

00:15:05.078 --> 00:15:06.831
So, I've lined up around
40 or 50 YouTubers

00:15:06.831 --> 00:15:09.760
who profiled my book, just
by having a simple outreach

00:15:09.760 --> 00:15:11.169
on related books.

00:15:11.169 --> 00:15:12.836
And the third thing to
do, around marketing,

00:15:12.836 --> 00:15:14.419
is really following up with the readers.

00:15:14.419 --> 00:15:17.442
You know, a lot of readers
don't even read the book,

00:15:17.442 --> 00:15:18.275
any book.

00:15:18.275 --> 00:15:19.465
Like, most people who will buy your book,

00:15:19.465 --> 00:15:20.445
it'll just sit there on the shelf,

00:15:20.445 --> 00:15:21.344
and they'll never read it.

00:15:21.344 --> 00:15:22.229
It just collects dust.

00:15:22.229 --> 00:15:25.215
And I would much rather sell ten books,

00:15:25.215 --> 00:15:27.287
and everybody read, those
ten people read the books,

00:15:27.287 --> 00:15:29.255
and sell 100, and nobody reads 'em.

00:15:29.255 --> 00:15:32.863
And so, having a way to
follow up, with readers,

00:15:32.863 --> 00:15:34.775
and making sure that they're
consuming the content,

00:15:34.775 --> 00:15:35.897
they need any help.

00:15:35.897 --> 00:15:37.146
And we do a lot of work.

00:15:37.146 --> 00:15:38.744
So, one of the things that we try to do,

00:15:38.744 --> 00:15:41.137
in the pre-campaigns, is collect emails.

00:15:41.137 --> 00:15:43.209
I wish I did something
stronger in the book.

00:15:43.209 --> 00:15:45.860
One of my regrets is, I
wish, like on the first page,

00:15:45.860 --> 00:15:50.483
it said, email your receipt
to this email address,

00:15:50.483 --> 00:15:52.986
and we'll send you
bonuses, because that way,

00:15:52.986 --> 00:15:54.851
you can collect a lot
more email addresses.

00:15:54.851 --> 00:15:56.705
And most of the people,
who bought my book,

00:15:56.705 --> 00:15:58.565
went through Amazon, and
I don't know who they are.

00:15:58.565 --> 00:16:00.164
So, I have no way of
following up with them.

00:16:00.164 --> 00:16:01.234
It's frustrating.

00:16:01.234 --> 00:16:02.790
But, we did collect a
lot of email addresses

00:16:02.790 --> 00:16:05.696
from our readers, and they
get put into a sequence,

00:16:05.696 --> 00:16:08.761
where every month, I'm
sending them an email,

00:16:08.761 --> 00:16:10.028
that's related to the book,

00:16:10.028 --> 00:16:11.981
that's asking them how they're
doing, that's checking in.

00:16:11.981 --> 00:16:13.536
Did you find your one word, can I help?

00:16:13.536 --> 00:16:15.169
Can I be your resource,
do you have any questions?

00:16:15.169 --> 00:16:16.408
Do you have any problems?

00:16:16.408 --> 00:16:18.339
I also send them a video of the month,

00:16:18.339 --> 00:16:19.880
that's answering somebody's question,

00:16:19.880 --> 00:16:22.526
so it's an unlisted video,
that you don't have access to,

00:16:22.526 --> 00:16:25.176
unless you bought the book,
and you get that once a month.

00:16:25.176 --> 00:16:28.055
And it'll also make a
customized video for everybody,

00:16:28.055 --> 00:16:30.785
and just a quick, ten second video.

00:16:30.785 --> 00:16:31.618
Hey, John.

00:16:31.618 --> 00:16:33.098
Thank you so much for picking up my book.

00:16:33.098 --> 00:16:34.371
I see you're from California.

00:16:34.371 --> 00:16:35.711
I really appreciate the support, man.

00:16:35.711 --> 00:16:37.940
I was just in California last month.

00:16:37.940 --> 00:16:39.783
If I come back again, it'll
be great to be able to connect

00:16:39.783 --> 00:16:41.147
and do something together.

00:16:41.147 --> 00:16:42.665
What's up, Jonathan?

00:16:42.665 --> 00:16:45.420
Alexandra, happy Tuesday.

00:16:45.420 --> 00:16:46.484
What's up, man?

00:16:46.484 --> 00:16:50.619
Greetings from Toronto,
all the way out to Jamaica.

00:16:50.619 --> 00:16:52.273
You know, just a quick personal video,

00:16:52.273 --> 00:16:53.729
and people really appreciate it.

00:16:53.729 --> 00:16:55.088
So, my goal is to follow up,

00:16:55.088 --> 00:16:57.757
because some people never
pick up a book, and read it.

00:16:57.757 --> 00:16:59.736
Or, some people, after the third message,

00:16:59.736 --> 00:17:01.033
they read it, they're right back,

00:17:01.033 --> 00:17:02.019
'cause they feel guilty,

00:17:02.019 --> 00:17:03.403
like oh, I haven't read the book yet.

00:17:03.403 --> 00:17:05.608
You want the people,
who've read your book,

00:17:05.608 --> 00:17:06.703
to spread it.

00:17:06.703 --> 00:17:08.487
Like, word of mouth is so important,

00:17:08.487 --> 00:17:09.800
for an author trying
to get their book out,

00:17:09.800 --> 00:17:11.684
'cause you're not spending
money on Super Bowl

00:17:11.684 --> 00:17:12.517
commercials, right?

00:17:12.517 --> 00:17:14.293
You don't have a million
dollar ad campaign.

00:17:14.293 --> 00:17:16.731
And so, you want the people
to spread it for you.

00:17:16.731 --> 00:17:18.007
And if they haven't read the book,

00:17:18.007 --> 00:17:19.690
then they can't spread the message!

00:17:19.690 --> 00:17:21.326
And so, thinkin' about ways

00:17:21.326 --> 00:17:24.727
to collect people's email
addresses, put it in a book,

00:17:24.727 --> 00:17:26.187
give them bonuses.

00:17:26.187 --> 00:17:28.164
I also write in the book, if
you're havin' any problems

00:17:28.164 --> 00:17:29.444
finding your one word, email me.

00:17:29.444 --> 00:17:30.740
I put the email address in there,

00:17:30.740 --> 00:17:33.462
so people connect through
that method as well.

00:17:33.462 --> 00:17:37.219
And if you can get them,
finding value in the book,

00:17:37.219 --> 00:17:38.799
they're much more likely
to tell their friends.

00:17:38.799 --> 00:17:40.897
And so, those are three of
the ideas that I'm using

00:17:40.897 --> 00:17:42.689
for my book, Your One Word,

00:17:42.689 --> 00:17:45.184
and I encourage you to find ways,

00:17:45.184 --> 00:17:48.161
continue to market it, so
it's not just a one-off thing,

00:17:48.161 --> 00:17:49.838
launch date, and then you forget about it.

00:17:49.838 --> 00:17:51.795
So, those are my seven
tips on how to write a book

00:17:51.795 --> 00:17:52.628
for beginners.

00:17:52.628 --> 00:17:55.725
I made this video, because
nazem abdrabo asked me to.

00:17:55.725 --> 00:17:57.175
So, if you want me to cover a topic

00:17:57.175 --> 00:17:59.122
in a future Seven Ways video,

00:17:59.122 --> 00:18:00.493
there's a link in the description.

00:18:00.493 --> 00:18:01.718
You can go check it out there,

00:18:01.718 --> 00:18:04.171
and vote for your next favorite topic.

00:18:04.171 --> 00:18:05.004
I'd also love to know,

00:18:05.004 --> 00:18:05.837
what did you think of this video?

00:18:05.837 --> 00:18:06.899
What was your favorite tip?

00:18:06.899 --> 00:18:09.082
What was most applicable to your process?

00:18:09.082 --> 00:18:10.782
Is there an eight, nine,
ten, that I missed,

00:18:10.782 --> 00:18:12.390
that you want to add to the list?

00:18:12.390 --> 00:18:14.058
Please share down in the comments below.

00:18:14.058 --> 00:18:16.297
I'm really excited to
see what you have to say.

00:18:16.297 --> 00:18:17.635
I also wanted to give a quick shout out

00:18:17.635 --> 00:18:19.480
to the legendary Brian Tracy.

00:18:19.480 --> 00:18:21.403
Brian, thank you so much
for picking up a copy

00:18:21.403 --> 00:18:24.180
of my book, Your One Word,
and sharing your review,

00:18:24.180 --> 00:18:25.656
and posting to Twitter.

00:18:25.656 --> 00:18:26.640
It really means a lot to me,

00:18:26.640 --> 00:18:28.972
and I'm so glad that you enjoyed the book.

00:18:28.972 --> 00:18:30.517
So, thank you guys so much for watching.

00:18:30.517 --> 00:18:31.555
I believe in you.

00:18:31.555 --> 00:18:33.428
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself,

00:18:33.428 --> 00:18:35.520
and whatever your one word is.

00:18:35.520 --> 00:18:36.592
Much love.

00:18:36.592 --> 00:18:38.092
I'll see you soon.

